	'nuances' => array(
		'CONSISTENCY — one English term or label gets exactly ONE Spanish rendering everywhere: on the same page and across the whole site, in nav, mega-menu, cards, footer, forms, headings, breadcrumbs, buttons, alt text, <title>, og:title and meta description. If the body says «ensayo», the page title cannot say «prueba»; if the nav says «Equipo directivo», the footer cannot say «Liderazgo»; if one option in a filter set reads «Aeroespacial e industrial», no sibling may stay «Aerospace & industrials». Before emitting any member of a visible set (tabs, <option>s, filter chips, spec rows, FAQ headings) scan the whole set and make them agree. Two correct synonyms for one on-screen object two lines apart is a defect.',
